===persian===

هوای ابر را بلبل نداره
به جز شوق گل و سنبل نداره
نمی‌دونه اگه بارون نباره
گل پژمرده بوی گل نداره

۱۳۸۰

===machine===

The nightingale has no longing for the cloud
- only desire for the rose and hyacinth.
It doesn't know: if the rain doesn't fall,
the wilted flower has no flower's scent...

1380

===translation===

The nightingale has no use for clouds
just the rose and hyacinth.
It doesn't know: if the rain won't fall,
the wilted flower has no scent...

